  "diagnostics": [
    "The first launcher exited on stdin EOF before browser checks; a PTY-owned launcher then kept a live handle for the full fixture.",
    "Control+A initially did nothing because Chromium supplied a control character as text. DOM key identity plus modifiers gives the native interpreter its actual logical shortcut.",
    "The Editor::ExecuteCommand convenience alias initially deleted without beforeinput. Direct real menu/key EditorCommand execution restores the expected trusted event pair.",
    "Thirty-nine checks passed before a programmatic-value pixel mismatch exposed the cached background. Real inner-editor value and selection boundaries now invalidate that whole native snapshot.",
    "Helper loss initially retained stale images in all six fields even though keyboard fallback worked. Invalidating native text fields on the existing failure wakeup restores complete original engine drawing immediately; all six full rectangles change and trusted insertion/click remain functional.",
    "A control-session close after its externally owned browser stopped failed CDP discovery. The offline doctor found a healthy named daemon; later cleanup closes the control session before its owned browser.",
    "Host Apple Python lacked Pillow. Qualification used the already bundled Python/Pillow runtime without installing packages.",
    "Guest fstrim reclaimed 9.7GiB of unused sparse-disk blocks; observed host free space increased from 571MiB to 1.9GiB without deleting files."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One pinned Debian ARM64 Chromium build, scale 1 and fixed field dimensions. Other builds, Chrome/Vivaldi and derivatives are not established by this pin.",
    "Only themed plain/password webpage inputs are covered. Native intrinsic sizing, other text types, multiline/rich text, author styling, transforms and scaling remain open.",
    "Chromium mouse text selection currently uses its engine path. Native mouse/multiple-click/data-drag/context-menu bindings remain open.",
    "Clipboard/cut/paste web-event integration, native undo-menu routing, typing undo grouping, selection-event/direction details, IME/composition and accessibility remain open.",
    "Engine undo is tested through its existing command API, not native undo shortcut/menu routing. Unsupported native semantic edit commands are vetoed.",
    "Native fixture fonts lack some Unicode glyphs. Value/UTF-16 preservation and equality to the actual native image are qualified, complete glyph coverage is not.",
    "Cached-page/tab restoration, long validators/modal editing, broader layout and sustained performance need qualification.",
    "Browser application interfaces/address bars, derivative-specific frontends and GTK/Qt/KDE apps remain required."
  ]
}
